Project 3 — Nashville Housing Data Cleaning (SQL)
Summary

Cleaned and standardized a housing dataset for downstream analysis.

Objective

Fix missingness, standardize formats, remove duplicates, and reshape columns for analysis.

Approach

Converted SaleDate to date only

Repopulated missing PropertyAddress using ParcelId joins across rows

Split Property and Owner addresses into address, city, state using SUBSTRING, CHARINDEX, and PARSENAME

Converted SoldAsVacant bit to Yes/No

Removed duplicates using CTE + ROW_NUMBER

Dropped unused columns for a lean table

Key Results

Address completeness improved without blind deletion

Columns reshaped for cleaner joins and grouping

Duplicates removed, table footprint reduced

Skills

Data standardization, missing value handling, string parsing, deduplication with window functions.

How to run

Execute CodeDataCleaning.sql in SQL Server against NashvilleHousingData.
